!SDLSpin
========

Example 4: the spinning triangle through SDL2, in a resizable window. Escape or the close icon quits.

Built from sdl2.c in the riscos-mesa devkit's examples folder; read the
comments in that file to see how it works.

Needs: RISC OS 5, an ARMv7 or later processor (Raspberry Pi 2, 3 or 4,
or a Cortex-A8/A9/A15 board), and SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport
from PackMan.

Licence: MIT (see LICENCES.txt in the devkit). Mesa, UnixLib and the
other parts linked into the program have their own licences, listed in
the same file.
